    {
      "name": "places/ChIJxQLzBACpQjQR7aLkwWucdr0/reviews/Ci9DQUlRQUNvZENodHljRjlvT2xOdVpsOWtUakZTUTJFNVNWZ3hSa2QxVDNCRWVWRRAB",
      "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 個月前",
      "rating": 2,
      "text": {
        "text": "這家早餐店最大的問題就是份量太小，但價格卻相對很高。點了一個 115 元的漢堡，上桌時被那個迷你尺寸嚇到，裡面也只是很平凡的漢堡肉加蛋，吃完後完全沒飽。脆皮蛋餅吃起來口感很乾，並不是那種炸得酥脆的口感，有點失望。燉飯的味道很普通，吃起來有一種超商微波食品的感覺。整體來說，味道沒有亮點，份量與價格完全不成正比，在台北有更多CP值更高的早餐選擇，應該不會再回訪。\n\nThe biggest issue with Wanna Breakfast is the tiny portions combined with high prices. I ordered a burger for 115 TWD and was shocked by how small it was—just a basic patty and egg with no special flavor. The \"crispy\" egg crepe was actually just very dry, not the crispy texture I expected. The risotto also tasted quite average, reminiscent of a microwave meal from a convenience store. Overall, the taste doesn't stand out, and the value for money is very poor. There are plenty of better breakfast spots in Taipei with larger portions and lower prices. I won't be returning.",
        "languageCode": "zh-Hant"
      },
      "originalText": {
